
JOIN in SQL is used to combine rows from two or more tables based on a related column between them.

Types of JOINs

1. INNER JOIN → Returns matching rows only

2. LEFT JOIN (LEFT OUTER JOIN) → All rows from left + matched from right

3. RIGHT JOIN (RIGHT OUTER JOIN) → All rows from right + matched from left

4. FULL OUTER JOIN → All rows from both tables

5. CROSS JOIN → Returns Cartesian product (all combinations)

6. SELF JOIN → Table joined with itself





